 "description": "T-4616: accumulation order of pivot totals in a 2-D pivot, StdDev/Var totals, Product order, and Count/CountNums at inner-field subtotals and beside each other. D1 (27 records, R first seen Q X B, K first seen M Z A, three records per cell) and D2 (18 records) are searched with Python doubles so that the candidate row, column and grand totals differ (cell sums in display, reverse or ascending order; item-by-item record accumulation in display, reverse or ascending item order; record order and reverse). S1 Sum, S2 Sum+Average, S3 Average, S4 Sum transposed (K on rows), S5 Sum over D2, S6 Sum over D4. D4 (36 records, R first seen Q X B F N C) separates Var algorithms and orders: V1 Var and V2 StdDev 2-D, V3 rows K and V4 rows R one-axis. D5/D6: Product over K, P1/P2, separating display item order from ascending value order and record order. D3: East A (Err 10), East B (#N/A), East A (3), West A (7), West B (5). I1-I4: rows Region and Kind, Count or CountNums of Err with or without Sum of Num. M1-M3: Count beside CountNums. Candidate values are in the task's Outcome and docs/excel-semantics/pivots.md. Pivot cells are in the sidecar's `pivots` section; Q!A1 makes the case scored.",
